# Errors, Logging, Memory

## Exceptions (`swcdb/core/Exception.h`)

- Throw: `SWC_THROW(code, msg)`, `SWC_THROWF(code, fmt, ...)`
- Assert: `SWC_EXPECT(expr, code)`, `SWC_ASSERT(expr)`
- Wrap/log current exception: `SWC_LOG_CURRENT_EXCEPTION(scope)` (defined in Exception.h)
- Daemon `run()` often uses `SWC_TRY_OR_LOG` to log and continue

Do not catch-and-swallow without logging. Prefer `SWC::Error::Exception` over bare `std::exception` throws.

## Logging (`swcdb/core/Logger.h`)

- `SWC_LOG(priority, message)`, `SWC_LOGF(priority, fmt, ...)`
- Fatal: `SWC_LOG_FATAL` / `SWC_LOG_FATALF`
- Priorities: `LOG_FATAL` … `LOG_DEBUG`

## Memory

- RAII via `shared_ptr` / `Ptr`; avoid raw `delete` in application code
- Factories commonly `new` into a `Ptr`; rely on smart-pointer lifetime
- Respect existing `SWC_CAN_INLINE` / move-only class patterns
